    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d23-a2">

                <pb facs="d23-05" n="5" xml:id="d23-05"/>


                <head>Memorandum from James E. Connor to the Director of the Office of Management
                    and Budget (Lynn)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1976-07-06"
                        >July 6, 1976</date>
                </dateline>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT:</label>
                    <item>P.L. 480 PROGRAMMING TRENDS</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President reviewed your memorandum of June 21 on the above subject and made
                    the following decisions:</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#underline">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Afghanistan:</hi>
                    </hi>
                </p>
                <p>Option #1—Undertake the proposed $2.6 million oil program and leave open the
                    possibility of future continuation.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#underline">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Jamaica:</hi>
                    </hi>
                </p>
                <p>Option #2—Do not undertake the program.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#underline">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Proliferation:</hi>
                    </hi>
                </p>
                <p>The following notation was made by the President regarding your recommendation
                    for OMB to undertake an interagency study to develop firm guidelines for future
                    Title I food aid programmin for political and developmental purposes for review
                    and approval by the beginning of Fiscal Year 1977.</p>
                <p>“New OMB study not essential now.”</p>
                <p>Please follow-up with appropriate action.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
